       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults is 3,200 mg/day, so this is twice that.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg per dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot. The patient's normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove those risks.\n\nWas this a typo, or did you mean something else? Some possible intended orders:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. I can enter it with a note if you confirm."
